---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { VERSION } from '../../data/site';
---

<Guide
  title="Versioning"
  description="Every @kyralabs package follows semantic versioning from 1.0.0 and shares one version number (DECISIONS D16)."
>
  <p>
    The current version is <strong>{VERSION}</strong>. All <code>@kyralabs/*</code> packages
    release together with the same version, so <code>@kyralabs/m3exp-web@{VERSION}</code> pairs
    with <code>@kyralabs/m3e-tokens@{VERSION}</code>, <code>@kyralabs/m3e-react@{VERSION}</code>
    and the rest.
  </p>

  <h2 id="within-1x">What changes within 1.x</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Minor releases</strong> add components, tokens, package entries and options.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Patch releases</strong> fix bugs and fidelity: behavior or pixels moving closer to
      the pinned Jetpack Compose source or m3.material.io. A fix that adds API is a minor release.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A source pin bump</strong> (a newer Compose Material3) is a minor release if no
      token name disappears; otherwise it waits for 2.0.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="breaking">What waits for 2.0</h2>
  <p>Anything that breaks a consumer:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      removing or renaming an export, package entry, CSS class, part or modifier, custom property,
      attribute or event;
    </li>
    <li>changing a component's DOM contract;</li>
    <li>raising a peer-dependency floor (React is 18.3+ or 19).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A renamed API keeps its old name until 2.0. The old name is marked <code>@deprecated</code>,
    and in React it warns once in development. The deprecated Material 3 components (DECISIONS D4)
    are also removed in 2.0.
  </p>

  <h2 id="depend">Depending on it</h2>
  <p>
    A caret range such as <code>^{VERSION}</code> takes every compatible release. Keep all
    <code>@kyralabs/*</code> packages on the same version: they are released and tested together.
    Each package's <code>CHANGELOG.md</code> lists what changed.
  </p>
</Guide>
